 "description": "Starting points for Mix Check. Monitoring: stereo, mono sum, left, right and side only (at full level, the side signal is already the weakest part of a mix), three quiet-listening levels (-6, -12 and -18 dB) and a level-matched reference. Situations: how a mix survives a mono club or PA (against the reference), a radio or kitchen speaker, a phone speaker, a car where you mostly hear the nearest speaker and a neighbouring room, each as a mono or one-sided monitor at a fitting level; the presets marked 'matched' also play the reference (Reference input or loaded file) at the same loudness as your mix, all others leave the reference level alone.",
